{
  "id": "80528",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Reaction Mechanisms",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The balanced equation for a chemical reaction indicates what reacts and what is produced, but it reveals no information regarding what actually happens on a molecular level during the reaction. Chemical reactions usually do not occur as a single step but rather as a series of steps that sum to the overall reaction equation. A "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "reaction mechanism"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A sequence of elementary steps describing how a reaction occurs at a molecular level."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "445397662",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "756951956",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " is the sequence of chemical steps that describe in detail how a reaction occurs, such as the relative orientations of reactants and the order in which bonds are broken and formed."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p0lyhoy6o667sl3",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Consider the decomposition of ozone, O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": ", into diatomic oxygen, O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", in the stratosphere:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "jopmbg03rojlngu",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "7i0wyxiunwu0ipb",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "08sjjhwmrbnd8m5",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm O}_3(g)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;3\\;{\\mathrm O}_2(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Although the overall equation for this reaction indicates that two molecules of ozone react to give three molecules of oxygen, the mechanism of the reaction does not involve the collision and reaction of two ozone molecules. Instead, the decomposition of O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " into O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " appears to follow a mechanism with two steps. In step 1, an O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " molecule absorbs ultraviolet radiation from the sun and decomposes into an O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " molecule and an O atom. In step 2, the O atom combines with another O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " molecule to form two O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " molecules:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "qxt4k3hdj715hom",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "8129r885t37djzs",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "k83li45o0hbewto",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{Step}\\;1:\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;{\\mathrm O}_3(g)\\;\\;\\rightarrow\\;\\;{\\mathrm O}_2(g)\\; +\\;\\mathrm O(g)\\;\\;\\\\\\underline{\\mathrm{Step}\\;2:\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm O(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm O}_3(g)\\;\\;\\rightarrow\\;\\;2\\;{\\mathrm O}_2(g) \\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\\\\\mathrm{Overall}:\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;2\\;{\\mathrm O}_3(g)\\;\\;\\rightarrow\\;\\;3\\; {\\mathrm O}_2(g)\\end{array}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Each individual step in a reaction mechanism is called an "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "elementary step"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "One step in a series of simple reactions that show the progress of a reaction at the molecular level. Also called an "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "elementary reaction"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ". "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "459306821",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "701995831",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " (or elementary reaction). An elementary step describes a single molecular event, such as a molecule decomposing or two particles combining. It occurs exactly as written and cannot be broken down into simpler steps. The elementary steps in a mechanism "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "must"
              },
              {
                "text": " add up to the overall reaction, which for the decomposition of ozone is 2 O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "g"
              },
              {
                "text": ") → 3 O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "g"
              },
              {
                "text": ")."
              }
            ],
            "id": "ne3ixy87ilmk866",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Notice that the oxygen atom produced in the first step of this mechanism is consumed in the second step and therefore does not appear in the overall reaction. Species that are produced in one step and consumed in a subsequent step are called "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "intermediates"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Species produced in one elementary step of a reaction and consumed in another step."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "560840399",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "207698998",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "gdb0c21uc24gi4l",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The energy profile for this reaction is similar to those we have seen previously but with an activation energy \"hump\" for each step."
              }
            ],
            "id": "97c1mqz6guj0q97",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "alt": "Alt text goes here",
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "The curve represents the energy of the system as the reaction progresses from the reactant O"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": " to the product O"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": ". The activation energy for step 1 is represented by E"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "doublesub": true,
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "1"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": ", and the activation energy for step 2 is E"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "doublesub": true,
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": ". The first peak represents the transition state for step 1, and the second peak is the transition state for step 2."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "40u0y0d2bs39ipc",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "3paotlix3iy178q",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/56/56c0561c560acb6801978fa1bf49aeb7/ozone_decomp_eneergy_profile.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "600"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "3045171895",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "1088293670",
